You're really almost there without poly-piling.  But to your question
I usually do polypile just to save time, and because it's fun.  I know
it's frowned upon by the purists, but in my mind if the game allows it
then it's fair.  Besides, there are penalties for over-piling.  My
favorite place to do it is Croesus' castle, after I've made huge piles
of the soldiers' belongings.

My strategy is to collect uni-horns throughout the entire game and go
for markers.  I also collect every scroll and potion along the way and
stash them, then go back to poly them for useful things.  I dilute
every useless potion for holy water and stash it for the return trip.
A pile of enchant-armor scrolls is a nice thing to have.  And one of
my sayings is: there's no such thing as too much holy water.



